 The entry point. The wasm build never calls it -- the shim exports renderFrame
 and walks `frame-at` itself -- but the emitter only emits what the entry can
 REACH (B6), so opening has to touch every name the shim calls or they are shaken
 out of the program and the wasm build fails on undeclared identifiers.

 That is not hypothetical here: the sky, horizon and sun never enter the draw
 buffer at all, because blitter.js paints them itself and only asks the module for
 the numbers. Nothing else reaches them. Touching them below is the whole reason
 they survive into the module.

 THE TRUCK'S MOTION IS THE SECOND INSTANCE AND IT IS EXACTLY THE SAME SHAPE. The
 shim steps the chase itself -- `truck-initial` at the start line, `truck-next`
 once a frame against the rider's route distance -- and no Codex caller reaches
 either, because the drawing side takes a position rather than computing one. Both
 names, and the `route-distance` and `course-length` the step needs, are touched
 below so that they exist to be called.

 It doubles as a native smoke test: run this on the host and it says how many
 commands each point of the sweep holds, which is the fastest way to see whether a
 frame is empty before ever opening a browser.

 We say:

Section: Entry

  report : Real -> Text
  report (u) =
    let sun = if (scene-sun-at u).visible then "sun on " else "sun off"
    in "seg " & show (drive-pos-at build-world u).seg & " sky " & show (sky-color (scene-step-at u)) & " horizon " & show (horizon-color (scene-step-at u)) & " " & sun & " x " & show (real-to-int (scene-sun-at u).x) & " cmds " & show (list-length (frame-at u))

  opening : [Console] Nothing = act
    print-line-uni ("cmds  " & show (list-length frame))
    print-line-uni ("rider " & show (list-length (frame-for build-world initial-rider-state truck-initial 0.0)) & " cmds at the start line, tilt e-3 " & show (real-to-int (initial-rider-state.tilt * 1000.0)) & " sun-x at step 0 " & show (real-to-int (sun-pos (heading-for initial-rider-state) 0.0 focal camera-w).x) & " and at 4000 " & show (real-to-int (sun-pos (heading-for initial-rider-state) 4000.0 focal camera-w).x) & " finished " & (if is-finished initial-rider-state build-world then "yes" else "no") & " next-v e-3 " & show (real-to-int ((get-next-rider-state initial-rider-state build-world).v * 1000.0)))
    print-line-uni ("m/frame " & show (real-to-int (u-per-step * 100000.0)) & " e-5 of the course")
    print-line-uni ("truck " & show (real-to-int truck-initial.pos) & " m ahead at the line, and after one frame " & show (real-to-int (truck-next truck-initial (route-distance build-world initial-rider-state.segment initial-rider-state.along) build-world (course-length build-world)).pos) & " m, over a course of " & show (real-to-int (course-length build-world)) & " m")
    print-line-uni ("u=0.00 " & report 0.0)
    print-line-uni ("u=0.25 " & report 0.25)
    print-line-uni ("u=0.50 " & report 0.5)
    print-line-uni ("u=0.75 " & report 0.75)
    print-line-uni ("u=1.00 " & report 1.0)
  end
